th angular velocities {$\omega$}o{$\approx-$}0.4{$\omega$}i{$\omega$}o{$\approx-$}0.4{$\omega$}i\textbraceleft\textbackslash omega \textbraceright\_\textbraceleft o\textbraceright{} \textbackslash approx - 0. 4\textbackslash hspace\textbraceleft 0.167em\textbraceright{} \textbraceleft\textbackslash omega \textbraceright\_\textbraceleft i\textbraceright{} . In contrast, for ReS{$\leq$}4\texttimes 103ReS{$\leq$}4\texttimes 103R\textbraceleft e\textbraceright\_\textbraceleft S\textbraceright{} \textbackslash leq 4\textbackslash times 1\textbraceleft 0\textbraceright\textasciicircum\textbraceleft 3\textbraceright{}  the torque features a maximum for a stationary outer cylinder. In addition, the effective torque scaling exponent is shown to also depend on the mean rotation state. Finally, we evaluate a close connection between boundary-layer thicknesses and the torque.},
