er. The behaviour of the latter term seems to follow some remarkable self-similarity trends towards high Reynolds numbers. A spectral analysis of the weighted Reynolds stress with respect to the distance to the wall and to the wavelength is provided for the first time to our knowledge and allows us to analyse the influence of the largest scales on the skin friction. It is shown that structures with a streamwise wavelength                                                                {$\lambda$}x{$>\delta\backslash$}lambda \_x {$>\backslash$}delta                                     contribute to more than                                                                60\%60\textbackslash, \textbackslash\%                                    of                                                                Cf,2C\_\textbraceleft f,2\textbraceright{}                                   , and that those larger than                                                                {$\lambda$}x{$>$}2{$\delta\backslash$}lambda \_x {$>$}2\textbackslash delta                                     still represent approximately                                                                45\%45\textbackslash, \textbackslash\%                                    of                                                                Cf,2C\_\textbraceleft f,2\textbraceright{}                                   .},
